{"nodes": [{"id": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_document", "label": "Roll Up / Roll Back SNARK Side Chain ~17000 TPS (ethresear.ch 2018)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "references/snowball/book/ref-136-roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://ethresear.ch/t/roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps/3675", "captured_at": "2026-06-14", "author": "BarryWhitehat, Alex Gluchowski, HarryR, Yondon Fu, Philippe Castonguay", "contributor": null}, {"id": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_zk_rollup", "label": "zk-Rollup (Roll_up Construction)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "references/snowball/book/ref-136-roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://ethresear.ch/t/roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps/3675", "captured_at": "2026-06-14", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Operator aggregates off-chain user transactions into a single on-chain SNARK-verified state update over a Merkle tree, so gas per state transition is constant regardless of transaction count; scalability is bounded by economically provable SNARK size (~60k constraints/tx, ~17000 tps estimated) rather than gasBlockLimit/gasPerTx."}, {"id": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_roll_back", "label": "Roll Back Mechanism", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "references/snowball/book/ref-136-roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://ethresear.ch/t/roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps/3675", "captured_at": "2026-06-14", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If data becomes unavailable the operator is replaced and the chain rolls back to a previously valid state, exiting users on request along the way; because SNARKs disallow invalid state transitions, recovery from a malicious operator does not force all users to exit, unlike Plasma's competitive mass-exit withdrawals. Leaves already exited can never exit again, preventing double withdrawal across rollbacks."}, {"id": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_priority_queue_exit", "label": "Priority Queue Exit", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "references/snowball/book/ref-136-roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://ethresear.ch/t/roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps/3675", "captured_at": "2026-06-14", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Users request withdrawals at the smart-contract level; if the operator fails to serve the queue within a time limit, data is assumed unavailable and the operator is slashed. This forces the worst case (malicious operator) to degrade to an on-chain token where funds cannot be stolen or withheld for meaningful time."}, {"id": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_operator_auction", "label": "Operator Auction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "references/snowball/book/ref-136-roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://ethresear.ch/t/roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps/3675", "captured_at": "2026-06-14", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "After slashing, a replacement operator is chosen by auction: bidders post a deposit and the state they wish to resume from; the highest bid on the most recent sidechain state wins. Operators need only be rational, not honest \u2014 bidding on newer states is advantageous, and a minimum stake deters repeat misbehavior."}, {"id": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_data_availability", "label": "Data Availability", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "references/snowball/book/ref-136-roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://ethresear.ch/t/roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps/3675", "captured_at": "2026-06-14", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only way the operator can cheat is by withholding data; users should not accept a transfer unless chain data is available, and a new operator should only join from a state for which they possess all data, or they risk being slashed by an unserviceable priority-queue request."}, {"id": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_snark_state_transition", "label": "SNARK-Verified State Transition", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "references/snowball/book/ref-136-roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://ethresear.ch/t/roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps/3675", "captured_at": "2026-06-14", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The operator proves that (previous state + set of transactions) produces the new state; the proof is verified inside the EVM and the Merkle root updated only if valid. The SNARK compresses signatures \u2014 explicit signatures need not be posted because the proof is implicit evidence they exist."}], "edges": [{"source": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_document", "target": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_zk_rollup", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "references/snowball/book/ref-136-roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_document", "target": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_roll_back", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "references/snowball/book/ref-136-roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_document", "target": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_priority_queue_exit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "references/snowball/book/ref-136-roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_document", "target": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_operator_auction", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "references/snowball/book/ref-136-roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_document", "target": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_data_availability", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "references/snowball/book/ref-136-roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_document", "target": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_snark_state_transition", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "references/snowball/book/ref-136-roll-up-roll-back-snark-side-chain-17000-tps.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_snowball_book_ref_136_roll_up_roll_back_snark_side_chain_17000_tps_roll_back", "target": "references_snowball_book_ref_13